      "hints": [
        "At the stationary point $(2, -3.5)$, set $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 0$.",
        "Substitute $x = 2$ and solve for $k$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Set $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 0$ at the stationary point $x = 2$:\n$$6(3(2) - 5)^3 - k(2^2) = 0$$",
        "Simplify and solve for $k$:\n$$6(6 - 5)^3 - 4k = 0 \\implies 6(1)^3 - 4k = 0 \\implies 4k = 6 \\implies k = \\frac{3}{2} = 1.5$$"
